A||N||9||Ronnie||Pulling up engine codes||||9||
Z||000000||Ronnie||05-23-2001||05:29 PM||||I've ran a search but nothing is pulling up at the moment.So, I've tried the paper clip, and I've tried a jumper wire, but I'm not getting anything!!! Somebody please tell me how to do this. It's like I'm not getting a good connection or something. Help????||||reg||9
Z||000001||beer_stud_21||05-23-2001||05:35 PM||||Disconnect the battery for a minute or two, then jumper the bottom two pins in the passenger side of the connector behind the cig lighter.  Turn the key to "on" and watch the engine light.  You will get a 1-2, 1-2, 1-2 then any codes (in pairs), then a 1-2, 1-2, 1-2. again.  if you get nothing but 12's then you have no codes.  <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000002||85Josh||05-23-2001||05:40 PM||||Actually, disconnecting the battery will clear out the codes. If shorting the A-B terminals dosen't cause the check engine light to flash, then check the bulb, it may be burned out. Does the light come on when you turn the key to "on"(withoput shorting the terminals)? If not, then the bulb is out.<P>------------------<BR>85 2M4(Lil' Bit)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ronnie||05-23-2001||06:18 PM||||Check engine light bulb is not blown - it's on that's why I'm running (trying) a code on it.  HELP!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||fyerstarter||05-23-2001||07:38 PM||||Are you sure the key is in the "on" position while your doing this? Also your jumping the two leads closest to the passenger seat right?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ronnie||05-23-2001||09:07 PM||||Got It!! I was jumping the wrong terminals.<BR>Got a Code 24. Throttle Speed Sensor. Not sure now exactly what to do , but, it said to check ECM connection and Throttle position sensor connection. Thanks guys.<BR>At least now I know how to do the diagnostic anyway.||||reg||6
Z||000006||PBJ||05-23-2001||09:14 PM||||code 24.  is for vehicle speed sensor. vss.  and are you sure its not 42.  which is electronic spark timing?<P>does your Speedo work ok??||||reg||1
Z||000007||Vlad||05-24-2001||03:53 AM||||Sometimes, the VSS code on Auto tranny cars may indicate that TCC is going bad. Keep you eye on it if you have auto tranny.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ronnie||05-24-2001||04:18 PM||||This is on my 86GT which is a 4 spd. But when it gives this code, it really starts running rough. Like , it won't take full throttle , so I have to limp home at partial throttle.<BR>I checked the connection on the throttle position sensor like the Haynes book said , and I cleared the code out. No problem , today anyway<P>------------------<BR>'86GT/'88FORMULA/'88GT<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ronnies_1.jpg"> ||||reg||6
Z||000009||Posthumane||05-24-2001||04:39 PM||||I was getting the same thing on my 84 2m4 SE, check engine would come on at idle sometimes, and it gave ma a code 24, and i got lots of stumbling under heavy throttle. I also had a bad thermostat which was causing the engine to run hot, and when i replace the thermo, the stumbling stopped.||||reg||1
